{"ticker":"ERIS","symbol":"ERIS","instrumentId":3151591,"name":"Eris Lifesciences","industry":"NSE-Medical-Biomed/Biotech","about":"Eris Lifesciences Ltd. is a top player in India's pharmaceutical sector, focusing on chronic and sub-chronic diseases like diabetes and cardiac care, which account for 86% of its revenue. The company’s flagship diabetes care therapy contributes 28% to its revenue, while cardiac care and VMN categories add 19% and 16%, respectively. With emerging therapies like Dermatology and Neuropsychiatry contributing 29% of revenue, Eris is diversifying its portfolio. The company operates a fully integrated business model with manufacturing facilities in Guwahati and Gujarat, serving a vast distribution network of 2,000+ stockists and 500,000+ chemists across India. Eris achieved a consolidated revenue of INR 16,851 million in FY23.","website":"www.eris.co.in","location":"INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:18:49.881Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":1329,"changePct":-0.6057886470720147,"week52High":1701.3,"week52Low":1095.5},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹18,438 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹3,330 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"62,432,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"172"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"35,988,762"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.54%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"4.72"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"1.4"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"24.0%"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"-0.07"},{"label":"Beta","value":"0.67"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"7%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"25.83"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"23–67"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"15.9%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"38.83"},{"label":"Volume","value":"28,428"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"116,961"},{"label":"Master score","value":"59"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"69"},{"label":"Price strength","value":"50"},{"label":"Group rank","value":"64